WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Good morning, Hank. It's Sunday.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.500
On Tuesday I'm going to announce your punishment

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.880
and discuss the political situation in Pakistan,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.800
but today we discuss a matter of pressing international importance:

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.200
The Twilight Saga

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.020
*Theme Plays*

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:22.200
So Hank before I begin discussing Twilight, I have to give the guys of Nerdfighteria, all 42 of you, a brief summary of the series.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.200
Ok, so there's a new girl in school and boy does her blood smell good!

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.900
Which, of course, would be irrelevant to most of us but most of us aren't Edward Cullen, hot, hot, hot, vampire.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.200
Edward Cullen looks like he's 17, but he's 107 years old and he's a vampire, so he's dangerous,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.220
but he's also very chivalrous because he comes from the old school, because he's 107 years old.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:46.600
And he's beautiful, and his eyes change color, and he's got super sexy puff. Also he sparkles when he's in the sunshine.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:53.940
And apparently this is what girls want us to be: Sparkly, non-farting, 107 year olds in 17 year old bodies.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.760
So anyway then this 107 year old gets in a relationship with a 16 year old girl which for some reason isn't wrong.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:06.160
Now Hank, before I talk about how much I love Twilight,
I want to explain why it's wrong for adults to have romantic relationships with teenagers.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.500
It's not because we look old. It's because we are old.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:17.000
It's not a question of the young-ness and chiseled-ness of your pecs, It's a question of how many times you've been around the sun.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:24.120
Also in the Twilight books this girl Bella really needs dudes to take care of her, because she is like completely crazy without them.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:31.640
And you almost get the feeling from reading the books that like a woman can't be whole until she has a strong, independent man in her life to take care of her.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:36.320
When, of course, the fact is a woman needs a strong man to take care of her like a fish needs a bicycle.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.000
I mean just ask the yeti: 
Hey Sarah!

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:38.900
Yeti: Yeah?

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:45.220
John: Do you need a man who can bench press your body weight in order to feel whole?

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.900
Yeti: Obviously not.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.280
*laughs*

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.480
"Obviously not"

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.280
And that's not because she's a big girl either.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:02:01.740
All that said, now and again a fantasy world comes along that is so engrossing and exciting and intoxicating that you never even stop to think like:

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.140
– Isn't it a little bit, you know, criminal for 107 year olds to have relationships with 16 year old girls?

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.200
And for me and millions others such is the case with Twilight.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.160
You just wanna keep turning the pages because while you're reading the books, nothing matters more to you

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.900
than the question of whether of not they will finally, you know, do it.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.580
There I said it!

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:25.000
And yes I think Edward and Bella's relationship dynamics are troubling and that you shouldn't conflate obsession with love.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.360
But we all romanticize the people we adore, particularly in high school,

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:34.120
and Edward Cullen and Jacob Black are both really well idealized romantic others.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.760
And by well idealized romantic others I, of course, mean that they are hot.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:43.480
So hank, I just saw New Moon, the movie, and to be honest I thought it was kinda stupid, but it reminded me what I really do like about Twilight.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.980
It's fun, it distracts me from the pain and brokenness of the world, and it argues that true love will triumph in the end.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.320
Which may or may not be true, but if it's a lie
it's the most beautiful lie we have.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:59.100
That's why I think the question of whether Harry potter or Twilight is better is, as the Buddhists would say; a&nbsp;question wrongly asked.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:06.080
As series, I don't think they're after the same goals, and I like to think that we could read broadly enough to live in a world that includes both of them and more.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.020
You know, like my books.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:16.180
So Hank that's my review. I think the books are insanely fun to read, I thought the movie was pretty stupid, although Jacob Black is insanely V-shaped in his torso.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:22.260
I'm sure the conversation will continue in comments. Nerdfighters, don't forget to be awesome. Hank, I will punish you on Tuesday.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:28.380
And yes, Hank, because I'm discussing Twilight today,
I left a button unbuttoned.

